1.d4 { WELCOME TO THE COLLE SYSTEM.

WHY THIS OPENING IS PERFECT FOR YOU RIGHT NOW:
You play almost the same seven moves in every single game. You do not need to memorise twenty different openings. You do not need to know what your opponent plays. You set up your pieces the same way, and then you attack.

Most players your level lose games in the opening because they do not know what to do. After this course, you will always know what to do.

THE SEVEN MOVES YOU MUST KNOW BY HEART:
d4, Nf3, e3, Bd3, Nbd2, O-O, and c3 (only when needed).
That is it. Learn these and you have an opening for life.

WHAT YOU WILL LEARN IN THIS COURSE:
- Lesson 1: The setup and the plan
- Lesson 2: The e4 break (this is how you win)
- Lesson 3: The bishop sacrifice on h7 (the knockout punch)
- Lesson 4-6: What to do when Black plays something else
- Lesson 7: The three mistakes that cost you the game

TIME NEEDED: about two hours. Then start playing it immediately. } 1...c6 2.c4 ( 2.e4 { take the whole center if given to you } ) 2...d5 3.Nf3 Nf6 4.Nc3 e6 5.Bg5 ( 5.e3 ) 5...h6 6.Bxf6 ( 6.Bh4 dxc4 7.e4 g5 8.Bg3 b5 9.Ne5 ( 9.Be2 Bb7 10.Ne5 ( 10.e5 Nd5 11.O-O ( 11.h4 g4 12.Nd2 Nxc3 13.bxc3 c5 14.a4 a6 15.dxc5 Bxg2 16.Rg1 Bd5 17.axb5 axb5 18.Rxa8 Bxa8 19.Bxg4 Bxc5 20.Qb1 Qa5 ) 11...a6 12.a4 c5 13.Ne4 Nd7 14.Nd6+ Bxd6 15.exd6 O-O 16.Ne5 cxd4 17.Nxd7 Qxd7 18.Qxd4 f6 19.axb5 axb5 20.Rxa8 Rxa8 21.Bf3 f5 22.Bxd5 Bxd5 23.Be5 Qb7 24.f3 Qa7 25.Qxa7 Rxa7 ) ( 10.h4 g4 11.Ne5 h5 12.O-O ( 12.f3 Nbd7 13.fxg4 ( 13.O-O Nxe5 14.Bxe5 Nd7 15.Bxh8 ( 15.Bg3 Be7 16.Qe1 Qb6 17.Rd1 e5 18.fxg4 exd4 19.Kh2 d3 20.Bf3 hxg4 21.Bxg4 Nf6 ) 15...g3 16.Qe1 ( 16.Rf2 Qxh4 17.Bxc4 gxf2+ 18.Kf1 bxc4 19.Ke2 O-O-O 20.d5 Bc5 ) 16...Qxh4 ) 13...hxg4 14.O-O Nxe5 15.Bxe5 Rh6 16.Bxg4 Nxg4 17.Qxg4 Qxh4 18.Qg8 Qh1+ 19.Kf2 Qh4+ 20.Ke3 Qh5 21.Rh1 Qg6 22.Qxg6 Rxg6 23.Rh8 Rh6 24.Rh1 Rxh1 25.Rxh1 Be7 26.Rh8+ Kd7 ) 12...Nbd7 13.b3 ( 13.Qc2 Nxe5 14.Bxe5 Bg7 15.Bg3 ( 15.b3 cxb3 16.axb3 O-O 17.Bg3 c5 18.dxc5 ( 18.e5 Nd5 19.Nxb5 cxd4 20.Nd6 Rb8 21.Rxa7 ( 21.Qd2 Nc3 22.Bd3 a5 23.Ra3 Bd5 24.Bc2 f5 25.exf6 Rxf6 ) 21...Nb4 22.Qd2 Bd5 23.Qxd4 ( 23.Ra3 d3 24.Bxd3 Nxd3 25.Qxd3 Bh6 26.Rb1 Rb4 ) 23...Qxd6 ) 18...Qd4 19.Bxb5 Nxe4 20.Nxe4 Bxe4 21.Qc4 ( 21.Qe2 Qxc5 22.Qxe4 Qxb5 ) 21...Qxc4 22.Bxc4 Bxa1 23.Rxa1 a5 24.Re1 Bd5 ) 15...O-O 16.e5 Nd5 17.Ne4 c5 18.Nd6 ( 18.Nxc5 Bc6 19.Rad1 Ne7 20.Rfe1 Nf5 ) 18...Qc7 19.dxc5 Qc6 20.Nxb7 Qxb7 21.b3 Qc6 22.bxc4 Qxc5 23.Rac1 bxc4 24.Bxc4 Bh6 25.Bxd5 Qxd5 26.Rfd1 Qa5 ) 13...Bb4 14.Qc2 cxb3 15.Qxb3 Bxc3 16.Qxc3 Nxe4 17.Qe3 Nxg3 18.fxg3 Nxe5 19.Qxe5 Rf8 20.Qxh5 Qxd4+ ) ( 10.O-O Nbd7 11.Ne5 ) 10...Nbd7 ) 9...Nbd7 10.Nxc6 ( 10.Be2 Bb7 11.O-O h5 12.Nxd7 ( 12.Nxf7 Kxf7 13.e5 ( 13.f4 h4 14.Be1 gxf4 15.e5 Nxe5 16.dxe5 Qxd1 17.Rxd1 Bc5+ 18.Kh1 Nd5 19.Ne4 ( 19.Nxd5 cxd5 20.Rxf4+ Ke8 21.Bxh4 Be3 22.Rg4 Kd7 23.Bf6 Rhg8 24.Re4 Bc5 25.h4 Kc7 26.Rg4 d4 ) 19...Be7 ) 13...h4 14.exf6 hxg3 15.fxg3 Nxf6 16.Ne4 Bg7 